meta-walky
==========

This Yocto layer contains the "walky" distribution: an embedded Linux
image running in kiosk mode, based on systemd and Wayland/Weston, with
automatic login and a graphical application launched directly on boot.

Dependencies
============

  URI: git://git.yoctoproject.org/poky
  branch: scarthgap

This layer only depends on the "core" layer provided by poky
(LAYERSERIES_COMPAT "scarthgap").

Patches
=======

Please submit any patches against the meta-walky layer to valentin.giaufer@gmail.com

Layer contents
==============

conf/distro/walky.conf
  Definition of the "walky" distribution (based on poky.conf): systemd
  as the init manager, PAM, usrmerge, and Wayland support.

recipes-core/images/walky-image.bb
  Main image, based on core-image-base, including:
    - SSH server (openssh)
    - Weston (+ examples) and Qt (qtbase, qtdeclarative)
    - a "walky" user (groups video, input, audio, render, tty)

recipes-core/base-files/base-files_%.bbappend
  Installs a kiosk .profile (profile-walky-kiosk) into /etc/skel, used to
  automatically start Weston on login.

recipes-core/systemd/systemd_%.bbappend
  Configures autologin on tty1 (autologin.conf) so the "walky" user is
  logged in automatically at boot.

recipes-graphics/weston/weston-init.bbappend
  Installs the Weston configuration (weston.ini) and a systemd drop-in
  unit (weston-user.conf). The weston.service/weston.socket service is
  intentionally disabled (SYSTEMD_AUTO_ENABLE = "disable"): Weston is
  started via /etc/skel/.profile (exec weston --socket=wayland-0)
  instead of through systemd.

Table of Contents
=================

  I. Adding the meta-walky layer to your build
 II. Notes

I. Adding the meta-walky layer to your build
=================================================

From the root of your Yocto build:

  bitbake-layers add-layer /path/to/meta-walky

Then build the image:

  bitbake walky-image

II. Notes
=========

- Layer compatible with the "scarthgap" Yocto release series.
- Kiosk mode relies on the combination of systemd autologin plus Weston
  being launched from the "walky" user's .profile, rather than through
  the weston.service systemd unit.
